<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-11.00%" pitch="-2.75%">
      As soon as their feet touch the water, everything changes.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The Jordan stops flowing.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The waters that were rushing south toward the Salt Sea simply stop.<break time="500ms"/>
      They rise up in a heap, far away, at a place called Adam.<break time="500ms"/>
      Miles upstream, the river gathers and holds itself still.<break time="1000ms"/>
      As if the hand of God reached down and pressed the current quiet.<break time="1800ms"/>

      And below that place, the riverbed empties.<break time="500ms"/>
      The water drains away.<break time="500ms"/>
      What was flood becomes dry ground.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Firm earth where moments before there was only rushing water.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The priests walk to the middle of the riverbed.<break time="500ms"/>
      They stand there, holding the ark, steady and still.<break time="500ms"/>
      The presence of God resting between them.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And they do not move.<break time="1800ms"/>

      All of Israel begins to cross.<break time="500ms"/>
      Family by family, tribe by tribe, they walk on dry ground through the middle of the Jordan.<break time="500ms"/>
      Children walk where the river ran.<break time="500ms"/>
      Old men cross where the flood once was.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The ground beneath their feet is firm and sure.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The priests stand in the centre, unmoved.<break time="500ms"/>
      Holding the ark.<break time="500ms"/>
      Holding the way open.<break time="1000ms"/>
      While the people pass safely through.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
